From 1ee8e9ad7776ddd5e7d150650602a74d1c5d77e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 02:40:31 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] escha vulkan: one hardware f32->f16 convert instead of the
 15-instruction software RTE

escha_F runs once per weight per token and dominated the kernel: the software
f32_to_f16_rte is ~15 instructions with three branches, against five for the rest
of the generator. AMD lowers packHalf2x16 to a single V_CVT_F16_F32, so the fast
path cuts the per-weight cost from ~21 instructions to ~7.

Guarded by ESCHA_HW_RTE (default 1, set 0 for the software path). The software
routine exists because Terra-66 measured that glslc does not emit float-control
execution modes, so the hardware rounding mode is a DEVICE FACT: this default is
only legitimate while the exhaustive 65,536-codeword sweep against the CPU
reference is GREEN on this device. That sweep is OWED before any speed claim
from this commit is quoted.

Origin: ArifiLabs (native)
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED at commit time - per-weight instruction count drops ~21 to ~7 by inspection; decode/prefill deltas and the exhaustive rounding sweep are owed
---
 .../ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/escha_mm.comp  | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/escha_mm.comp b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/escha_mm.comp
index c70661caf..d357e307a 100644
--- a/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/escha_mm.comp
+++ b/ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/escha_mm.comp
@@ -88,11 +88,30 @@ uint f32_to_f16_rte(float f) {
 }
 
 // the recovered cbA scalar generator F(x) on a 16-bit window
+//
+// PERF (HQ seat-38, 2026-08-21): this runs ONCE PER WEIGHT PER TOKEN and it dominated the kernel.
+// The software f32_to_f16_rte above is ~15 instructions with three branches; the rest of the
+// generator is five. AMD implements f32->f16 as a single V_CVT_F16_F32, which packHalf2x16 lowers
+// to, so the fast path replaces ~15 instructions with one. Kept behind a define because the whole
+// reason the software routine exists is Terra-66's finding that glslc does not emit float-control
+// execution modes -- so the hardware rounding mode is a DEVICE FACT to be proven, never assumed.
+//
+// ESCHA_HW_RTE=0 restores the software path. Do not flip the default back on taste: the fast path
+// is only legitimate while the exhaustive 65,536-codeword sweep against the CPU reference is GREEN
+// on this device (harness: trial-evidence/escha-decoder/rung1/run_sweep.py, the July rung-1 tool).
+#ifndef ESCHA_HW_RTE
+#define ESCHA_HW_RTE 1
+#endif
+
 float escha_F(uint xw) {
     const uint q = 0x3B603B60u ^ ((xw * 0xCBAC1FEDu) & 0x8FFF8FFFu);
     const vec2 h = unpackHalf2x16(q);
     const float s = h.x + h.y;                     // exact operands; correctly-rounded f32 add
+#if ESCHA_HW_RTE
+    return unpackHalf2x16(packHalf2x16(vec2(s, 0.0))).x;   // one hardware convert
+#else
     return unpackHalf2x16(f32_to_f16_rte(s)).x;    // value of the f16-rounded sum
+#endif
 }
 
 // 64-bit funnel shift via two u32s; no shaderInt64
